    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I'd like COBRA to estimate how smoking (coded 0/1) and age shape gene co-expression in our 400 airway brushings. We haven't decided whether to restrict the analysis to the 150 inflammation genes on our panel or use the 2,000 most variable genes."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I'd like COBRA to estimate how smoking (coded 0/1) and age shape gene co-expression in our 400 airway brushings.\" -- available from COBRA. Not stated in your request: COBRA needs more genes than samples -- checked against your files before any run.\n2. \"We haven't decided whether to restrict the analysis to the 150 inflammation genes on our panel or use the 2,000 most variable genes.\" -- not matched to any registered workflow.\n\n**COBRA**. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nYou would need expression matrix, sample covariate design matrix. The analysis would provide inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
